OL,3,GNEWSALives of Potteries women          
OL,4,Acelebrated in new book                 
OL,6,FHer story is featured in Ladies of the 
OL,7,FPotteries, a book by consultant        
OL,8,Fpsychiatrist Lisetta Lovett which tells
OL,9,Fthe stories of more than 30 women born 
OL,10,Fbefore 1953.                           
OL,12,F"There are lessons to be learnt from   
OL,13,Fthese ladies' memories and their       
OL,14,Fhard-earned experiences," the author   
OL,15,Ftold BBC Radio Stoke.                  
